# Workflow gates

- Read [prd/README.md](prd/README.md) before product work.
- **No product features** until it names an **active phase** and the relevant `prd/` doc exists.
- **No invented requirements** — ChatPRD + `prd/` only (not Superpowers `brainstorming`).
- **No application code** until `implement-from-prd` is run and the user approves the plan.
- **Scope:** implement only the active Linear issue / PRD section unless the user expands it.
- **Linear issues:** link `prd/…` + acceptance criteria; do not paste the full PRD.

# Before PR is ready for human review

Complete this checklist; summarize results in the PR description:

- [ ] `check-prd-alignment` vs linked `prd/` section (note gaps)
- [ ] Superpowers `code-reviewer` vs approved plan + [engineering.mdc](engineering.mdc)
- [ ] cursor-team-kit `deslop` on changed code (or N/A — docs-only)
- [ ] Tests/lint run, or state **CI not configured yet** and what was run manually
- [ ] PR: summary, risks, test plan, PRD deviations (if any)

Do not ask the human to review until the above is done.

